description: Do not credit Cursor or cursoragent on git commits or pull requests
alwaysApply: true
---

# Git attribution

Commits and pull requests in this repo are authored only by the human owner.

- Do not add `Co-authored-by` for Cursor, Cursor Agent, or `cursoragent@cursor.com`.
- Do not add `Made-with: Cursor`, `Made with Cursor`, or a `--trailer` that names Cursor.
- Do not set the commit author or committer to Cursor.

Cursor may still append a trailer after the commit command is written. Before pushing, read the new commit message. If it contains `cursoragent` or a Cursor attribution trailer, amend that unpushed commit and remove only those lines, then push. Do not amend a commit that is already on the remote.
